There are no "hpet" clocksource (and no acpi, as these are disabled in kernel):
  jiffies tsc pit

I selected "pit" (and later tsc) and the machine booted OK.
However, the precision is much worse than with 2.6.18-rt6. The simple
tool I use "timing.c" (do not have the url I found it right now), uses
100 threads to test timing. Aprox results:
rt6: <100 us (never worse than 280 us)
rt7 pit ~2ms
rt7 tsc ~1ms

I may add that I had completely disabled power management, as
recommended in the wiki, even if the config I previously sent included
APM.
Including the latest config.

Thanks!

/Gerhard

On 11/7/06, Darren Hart <dvhltc@us.ibm.com> wrote:
<snip>
